e\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is USDT0 on Stellar the same as USDT?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"USDT0 on Stellar is the USDT0 representation of USDT within the USDT0 Network. It keeps one unified USDT across supported chains instead of a separate bridged version with isolated liquidity. For users on Stellar, USDT0 works as the USDT asset available through the USDT0 system.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How are transfers to and from Stellar secured?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Transfers to and from Stellar are secured by LayerZero, the interoperability protocol behind USDT0, and by the USDT0 Attestation System. The Attestation System verifies every transfer through independent attestation before it finalizes. Each message needs sign-off from the Core Attestation Set, a 3-of-3 signer group of USDT0, LayerZero, and Canary. No single verifier can approve a transfer on its own. USDT0 moves with a burn-and-mint model and 1:1 backing: no wrapped tokens, no external bridges.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the fees to bridge to and from Stellar?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Moving USDT0 between Stellar and any other USDT0 Network chain has no protocol fee (0 bps). You only pay network gas on the source and destination chains. When the other side is a Legacy Mesh chain (native USDT on Solana, TON, Tron, and Celo), the transfer routes through the Legacy Mesh and costs 0.03% (3 bps), paid in USDT.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the USDT contract address on Stellar?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The Stellar USDT contract address is USDT0:GATISXX6BZ6NC7IKQBY37CJD4SOZL3CYZJWXEDG6JVIY4WBS6KXJHN6Q. This is the contract for the token you receive when you bridge USDT to Stellar through USDT0. Double-check the full address before sending funds.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which wallets does the USDT0 transfer widget support on Stellar?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"On Stellar, the USDT0 transfer widget supports Varial, LOBSTR, Bitget, and wallets that support WalletConnect.\"}}]}"])</script><script nonce="YmZmNDM5NmMtMDc5ZC00MTI2LThlMzktMTQ2NWRmNzEzMmFi">self.__next_f.push([1,"5:[\"$\",\"$L10\",null,{\"header\":[\"$\",\"$L11\",null,{}],\"hero\":[\"$\",\"$L12\",null,{\"network\":{\"name\":\"Stellar\",\"chainKey\":\"stellar\",\"logoDark\":\"/static/networks/logos/dark/stellar.svg\",\"logoLight\":\"/static/networks/logos/light/stellar.svg\",\"supportsUSDT\":true,\"supportsXAUT\":false}}],\"footer\":[\"$\",\"$L13\",null,{}],\"children\":[\"$L14\",\"$L15\",[\"$\",\"$L16\",null,{\"network\":\"$5:props:hero:props:network\",\"deliveredSymbol\":\"USDT0\"}],[\"$\",\"$L17\",null,{\"title\":\"How USDT0 Works on Stellar\",\"body\":[[\"USDT0 extends USDT to Stellar on one shared standard, so liquidity never splits into a separate bridged version. USDT0 on Stellar is the same asset across the whole network: no wrapped tokens, 1:1 backing. For users, exchanges, and applications, it works as USDT on Stellar and moves between chains in one step.\"]]}],[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$18\"}}],[\"$\",\"$L19\",null,{\"variant\":\"usdt0\",\"faqs\":[{\"question\":\"Is USDT0 on Stellar the same as USDT?\",\"answer\":\"USDT0 on Stellar is the USDT0 representation of USDT within the USDT0 Network. It keeps one unified USDT across supported chains instead of a separate bridged version with isolated liquidity. For users on Stellar, USDT0 works as the USDT asset available through the USDT0 system.\",\"id\":\"item-1\"},{\"question\":\"How are transfers to and from Stellar secured?\",\"answer\":\"Transfers to and from Stellar are secured by LayerZero, the interoperability protocol behind USDT0, and by the USDT0 Attestation System. The Attestation System verifies every transfer through independent attestation before it finalizes. Each message needs sign-off from the Core Attestation Set, a 3-of-3 signer group of USDT0, LayerZero, and Canary. No single verifier can approve a transfer on its own. USDT0 moves with a burn-and-mint model and 1:1 backing: no wrapped tokens, no external bridges.\",\"id\":\"item-2\"},{\"question\":\"What are the fees to bridge to and from Stellar?\",\"answer\":\"Moving USDT0 between Stellar and any other USDT0 Network chain has no protocol fee (0 bps). You only pay network gas on the source and destination chains. When the other side is a Legacy Mesh chain (native USDT on Solana, TON, Tron, and Celo), the transfer routes through the Legacy Mesh and costs 0.03% (3 bps), paid in USDT.\",\"id\":\"item-3\"},{\"question\":\"What is the USDT contract address on Stellar?\",\"answer\":\"The Stellar USDT contract address is USDT0:GATISXX6BZ6NC7IKQBY37CJD4SOZL3CYZJWXEDG6JVIY4WBS6KXJHN6Q. This is the contract for the token you receive when you bridge USDT to Stellar through USDT0. Double-check the full address before sending funds.\",\"id\":\"item-4\"},{\"question\":\"Which wallets does the USDT0 transfer widget support on Stellar?\",\"answer\":\"On Stellar, the USDT0 transfer widget supports Varial, LOBSTR, Bitget, and wallets that support WalletConnect.\",\"id\":\"item-5\"}],\"pt\":{\"xs\":12.5,\"md\":25}}]],\"$L1a\",\"$L1b\"]}]\n"])</script><script nonce="YmZmNDM5NmMtMDc5ZC00MTI2LThlMzktMTQ2NWRmNzEzMmFi">self.__next_f.push([1,"2:[\"$\",\"html\",null,{\"lang\":\"en\",\"style\":{\"colorScheme\":\"dark\",\"backgroundColor\":\"#0D0D0D\"},\"children\":[[\"$\",\"head\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"theme-color\",\"content\":\"#0D0D0D\",\"data-app-theme\":\"\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"ahrefs-site-verification\",\"content\":\"addb492dae652a35c32faca0973b209d65c826d14d9ba5648659e84f6bee1a89\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"body\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{